---
import { filmSettings } from '../data/film';
const film = filmSettings(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_FOUNDER_FILM_URL, import.meta.env.DEV && !!process.env.FILM_REVIEW_SOURCE);
---
<section id="film" class="template-film template-wrap">
        <div class="film-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">One expression of the idea</p><h3>A minute about the future we're imagining.</h3></div><span class="film-duration">60 seconds</span></div>
        {film.url ? <video class="founder-film" controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/dharmic-assets/founder-film-poster.svg" aria-label="Conscious Compute founder film, working cut" aria-describedby="film-status"><source src={film.url} type="video/mp4" /><track kind="captions" src="/dharmic-assets/founder-film-en.vtt" srclang="en" label="English draft captions" default />Your browser cannot play this video. Read the story below.</video> : <div class="film-poster"><img src="/dharmic-assets/founder-film-poster.svg" alt="Conscious Compute. A future we have a stake in. A 60-second film in progress." width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy" /><span class="film-pending">The film is being prepared for public viewing.</span></div>}
        <p id="film-status" class="source-note">{film.review ? 'Private review copy. This working cut is not creatively approved. The film-production goal remains paused.' : 'A film in progress. The school is the larger work.'}</p>
        <div class="film-context">
          <article><span class="eyebrow">The concept</span><p>America can build extraordinary AI and still fail to build a future its people have a stake in. The school is my response.</p></article>
          <article><span class="eyebrow">The inspiration</span><p>A caring idea made with friends, years of teaching, and the stories people have used to imagine a life worth living.</p></article>
          <article><span class="eyebrow">The significance</span><p>Making the film exposed the same problem we want to teach: AI can produce something faster than we learn to judge it.</p></article>
        </div>
        <a class="text-link" href="/learn#field-notes">Build shared context for your own team <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        <details class="film-transcript"><summary>Read the film's narration and visual context</summary><p class="source-note">Draft text alternative from the current narration script and edit record. It does not replace the independent sound and picture review.</p><div id="film-transcript-body"><p>Our idea was a call from your future self, helping you keep going. That&#x27;s what I love about teaching and building: imagination becoming useful to someone.</p><p>The prize gave me tools to keep building. America can build extraordinary AI and still fail to build a future its people have a stake in.</p><p>I&#x27;m building Dharmic Data. A school where people get paid to learn by building for their communities. Time to learn. Teachers beside you.</p><p>My bet is that a generation can become builders, owners and stewards of our AI future.</p><p class="source-note">Visual context: historical printing, Jai’s own imagery, a generated future-self call concept, an illustrative community classroom, the literature project and a NASA view of America at night. These images do not document an operating paid cohort or a clinical outcome.</p></div></details>
      </section>
